WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.300 --> 00:00:02.601
-Welcome, welcome,
welcome, welcome to

00:00:02.601 --> 00:00:03.667
"The Tonight Show," everybody.

00:00:03.667 --> 00:00:06.167
Thank you for watching.
I appreciate it.

00:00:06.167 --> 00:00:08.501
Thank you for being here.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:08.501 --> 00:00:10.000
Well, guys,
let's get to some news.

00:00:10.000 --> 00:00:13.234
Today, President Biden held
a big one-on-one video call

00:00:13.234 --> 00:00:15.300
with Russian president
Vladimir Putin

00:00:15.300 --> 00:00:17.100
that lasted two hours.

00:00:17.100 --> 00:00:19.434
And like most
two-hour meetings over Zoom,

00:00:19.434 --> 00:00:22.434
Putin was like,
"This could have been e-mail."

00:00:25.634 --> 00:00:27.300
On the bright side,
it was the first time

00:00:27.300 --> 00:00:28.901
Putin could see Biden on camera

00:00:28.901 --> 00:00:31.634
when Biden actually knew
he was on camera.

00:00:33.701 --> 00:00:35.467
Zoom meetings
with Putin are interesting.

00:00:35.467 --> 00:00:36.801
Some people go without pants.

00:00:36.801 --> 00:00:38.934
Putin just goes without a shirt.

00:00:38.934 --> 00:00:42.067
And a space background, too.

00:00:42.067 --> 00:00:43.400
I saw that,
before the big meeting,

00:00:43.400 --> 00:00:44.734
Biden spoke with the leaders of

00:00:44.734 --> 00:00:47.033
Germany, France, Italy,
and the U.K.

00:00:47.033 --> 00:00:48.534
That's not all.

00:00:48.534 --> 00:00:51.367
Several other European leaders
reached out to give him advice.

00:00:51.367 --> 00:00:52.868
Here's what they had to say.
Check this out.

00:00:52.868 --> 00:00:55.400
First, we have British
Prime Minister Boris Johnson.

00:00:55.400 --> 00:00:56.501
He told Biden...

00:01:00.200 --> 00:01:01.200
-Wow!

00:01:01.200 --> 00:01:02.868
-Not the advice --
-Yeah.

00:01:02.868 --> 00:01:04.367
-Not the advice
he was asking for.

00:01:04.367 --> 00:01:05.901
-Good advice, though.

00:01:05.901 --> 00:01:08.267
-Next, we have Irish president
Michael D. Higgins.

00:01:08.267 --> 00:01:09.400
He said...

00:01:13.033 --> 00:01:14.868
What is he...

00:01:16.133 --> 00:01:19.300
Next, we have
President Erdogan of Turkey.

00:01:19.300 --> 00:01:20.334
He told Biden...

00:01:28.000 --> 00:01:29.300
After that,
we have Italian president

00:01:29.300 --> 00:01:30.868
Sergio Mattarella.

00:01:30.868 --> 00:01:31.868
He said...

00:01:38.567 --> 00:01:40.067
What?

00:01:40.834 --> 00:01:45.033
Here's Scotland's
first minister, Nicola Sturgeon.

00:01:45.033 --> 00:01:46.033
She told Biden...

00:01:53.801 --> 00:01:55.767
And, finally,
President George Vella of Malta

00:01:55.767 --> 00:01:57.534
gave Biden some advice.

00:01:57.534 --> 00:01:58.601
He said...

00:02:02.968 --> 00:02:04.367
At least that's something.

00:02:05.634 --> 00:02:07.067
Well, this is going viral.

00:02:07.067 --> 00:02:10.901
China's moon rover spotted
a mysterious cube-shaped object

00:02:10.901 --> 00:02:13.133
on the moon's surface,
and everyone on the Internet

00:02:13.133 --> 00:02:15.434
is trying to figure out
what it is.

00:02:15.434 --> 00:02:16.868
And if there is
anyone who knows the truth,

00:02:16.868 --> 00:02:19.234
it's random people
on the Internet.

00:02:21.267 --> 00:02:22.434
Yeah, the same Internet

00:02:22.434 --> 00:02:25.267
that couldn't figure out
the color of a dress.

00:02:25.267 --> 00:02:27.701
[ Applause ]

00:02:27.701 --> 00:02:29.567
And they decided
what's on the --

00:02:31.234 --> 00:02:32.400
Hey, but this is cool.

00:02:32.400 --> 00:02:34.434
I just saw that Nicolas Cage
has been cast

00:02:34.434 --> 00:02:36.834
as Dracula in a new movie.

00:02:36.834 --> 00:02:40.000
And here now, on the phone, to
talk about it is Nicolas Cage.

00:02:40.000 --> 00:02:41.634
Nic. Nic, are you there?

00:02:41.634 --> 00:02:43.234
-Jimmy!

00:02:43.234 --> 00:02:48.100
It's my distinct honor
to be talking with you.

00:02:48.100 --> 00:02:50.701
-Thank you for being here.
So, you've been cast as Dracula?

00:02:50.701 --> 00:02:51.934
-It's true.

00:02:51.934 --> 00:02:55.000
I'm going to play
the King of the Bats.

00:02:55.000 --> 00:02:56.067
-That's great. That's great.

00:02:56.067 --> 00:02:58.868
-I never heard of Dracula
until yesterday.

00:02:58.868 --> 00:03:00.467
But get this, Jimmy.

00:03:00.467 --> 00:03:04.267
He's an old Russian guy who's
obsessed with wearing capes.

00:03:04.267 --> 00:03:06.767
That's kind of his whole thing.

00:03:06.767 --> 00:03:09.634
-I mean, I think there's more to
Dracula than his cape.

00:03:09.634 --> 00:03:13.367
-Hey! Want to hear me do
my Dracula, Jimmy?

00:03:13.367 --> 00:03:15.234
-Sure. Of course.
Let's hear it.

00:03:15.234 --> 00:03:16.367
-Okay. Here we go.

00:03:16.367 --> 00:03:17.434
[ Clears throat ]

00:03:17.434 --> 00:03:20.234
"Get that garlic away from me!

00:03:20.234 --> 00:03:24.167
It almost got on my cape."

00:03:24.167 --> 00:03:26.701
-That sounds great, Nic.
I don't know what to say.

00:03:26.701 --> 00:03:28.767
I can't wait to see this movie.

00:03:28.767 --> 00:03:32.167
-Jimmy, guess who's
gonna play Frankenstein?

00:03:32.167 --> 00:03:33.234
-I don't know. Who?

00:03:33.234 --> 00:03:36.100
-Ah, geez. I mean, oh, cool.

00:03:36.100 --> 00:03:37.434
I mean,
I just got struck by lightning.

00:03:37.434 --> 00:03:38.667
Now I'm, like,
all green and stuff.

00:03:38.667 --> 00:03:39.968
-Wow. Oh, my gosh.

00:03:39.968 --> 00:03:42.067
John Travolta is going to be
playing Frankenstein?

00:03:42.067 --> 00:03:44.000
-Yeah. Like,
I'm just, like, green freak --

00:03:44.000 --> 00:03:45.901
You know, I'm, like,
a freaky, green guy,

00:03:45.901 --> 00:03:47.300
like, eating brains
or something.

00:03:47.300 --> 00:03:49.534
-Let's get
one thing straight, Jack.

00:03:49.534 --> 00:03:51.634
Frankenstein
does not wear a cape.

00:03:51.634 --> 00:03:53.067
-Oh, come on, man.

00:03:53.067 --> 00:03:56.701
Just because I'm green doesn't
mean I can't wear a cape, right?

00:03:56.701 --> 00:03:57.868
-Back off!

00:03:57.868 --> 00:04:01.234
This is the Drac show,
and don't you forget it!

00:04:01.234 --> 00:04:03.167
-Aw, man, your voice is
kind of loud, right?

00:04:03.167 --> 00:04:05.501
I don't even know if I want to
do this movie no more.

00:04:05.501 --> 00:04:07.100
No way.
-Way.

00:04:07.167 --> 00:04:08.634
-No way.
-Way.

00:04:08.634 --> 00:04:11.434
-No way.
-I implore you, way.

00:04:11.434 --> 00:04:12.667
-No.
-Yes.

00:04:12.667 --> 00:04:13.701
-No, no.
-Yes, yes.

00:04:13.701 --> 00:04:14.701
-Just stop.

00:04:14.701 --> 00:04:15.901
-Just start.
-I'm going.

00:04:15.901 --> 00:04:16.934
-I'm coming.

00:04:16.934 --> 00:04:18.734
-No, thanks.
-Yes, you're welcome.

00:04:18.734 --> 00:04:20.100
-Goodbye.
-Hello.

00:04:20.100 --> 00:04:21.267
-No way.

00:04:21.267 --> 00:04:23.167
-Alright, look, guys,
just figure it out.

00:04:23.167 --> 00:04:25.167
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:27.067 --> 00:04:31.501
I hate to see two of
my favorite celebrities

00:04:31.501 --> 00:04:33.367
arguing like that on television.

00:04:33.367 --> 00:04:34.734
-A troll doll.

00:04:34.734 --> 00:04:38.667
-Hey, guys, in a new survey,
70% of American dog owners

00:04:38.667 --> 00:04:41.801
say that their dog
overeats during the holidays.

00:04:41.801 --> 00:04:43.667
Yeah. Then their dogs were like,

00:04:43.667 --> 00:04:45.167
"It's called
seasonal depression,

00:04:45.167 --> 00:04:47.334
and telling everyone
is not helping."

00:04:48.467 --> 00:04:49.968
You know your dog overeats
when he drops an

00:04:49.968 --> 00:04:53.100
Alka-Seltzer in the toilet bowl
before drinking, you know?

00:04:55.234 --> 00:04:56.567
Get this.

00:04:56.567 --> 00:04:59.400
A pub owner in the U.K.
claims that security footage

00:04:59.400 --> 00:05:03.100
from his bar shows proof of
supernatural activity.

00:05:03.100 --> 00:05:05.100
There's only one guy sitting at
the bar when it happens,

00:05:05.100 --> 00:05:06.968
so just watch the beer
next to him very closely.

00:05:06.968 --> 00:05:08.033
Watch.

00:05:08.033 --> 00:05:10.033
[ Indistinct conversations ]
♪♪

00:05:15.167 --> 00:05:17.300
-What's done that?

00:05:17.300 --> 00:05:18.801
That was very odd.

00:05:18.801 --> 00:05:20.567
Oh, my God.

00:05:20.567 --> 00:05:22.534
-Yeah.

00:05:22.534 --> 00:05:24.901
The pub was like, "Casper,
do we need to call your wife

00:05:24.901 --> 00:05:27.767
to come get you again?"

00:05:27.767 --> 00:05:28.834
That's laziest ghost
I've ever seen.

00:05:28.834 --> 00:05:29.901
Other ghosts are like,

00:05:29.901 --> 00:05:31.701
"I haunted a mansion
for 500 years."

00:05:31.701 --> 00:05:34.300
This guy is like, "Well,
I knocked over a glass once."

00:05:34.300 --> 00:05:35.534
Meanwhile, forget the ghost.

00:05:35.534 --> 00:05:37.801
The craziest thing a
that 7-year-old bartender.

00:05:37.801 --> 00:05:39.434
I like that guy.

00:05:41.767 --> 00:05:45.334
No one said anything about him.

00:05:45.334 --> 00:05:46.934
-"Here you go."

00:05:49.567 --> 00:05:51.801
-Finally, a man in England
spent months building

00:05:51.801 --> 00:05:54.167
the country's largest train set
in his basement

00:05:54.167 --> 00:05:57.467
while keeping it
a secret from his girlfriend.

00:05:57.467 --> 00:06:00.300
Officials think he's lying,
because no one has ever

00:06:00.300 --> 00:06:02.267
said the words "girlfriend"
and "model train set"

00:06:02.267 --> 00:06:03.434
in the same sentence.

00:06:03.434 --> 00:06:05.167
What a show we have
for you tonight.

00:06:05.167 --> 00:06:07.968
She stars in the new movie
"Mother/Android,"

00:06:07.968 --> 00:06:10.734
which is available on
Hulu December 17th.

00:06:10.734 --> 00:06:13.434
Chloe Grace Moretz
is here today.

00:06:13.434 --> 00:06:15.434
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:16.434 --> 00:06:18.434
Plus, he is one of my favorites.

00:06:18.434 --> 00:06:19.868
One of the funniest guys
out there.

00:06:19.868 --> 00:06:23.901
His "Known European" stand-up
tour kicks off later this month.

00:06:23.901 --> 00:06:27.067
And his new movie, "Mix Tape,"
is streaming now on Netflix.

00:06:27.067 --> 00:06:28.834
Nick Thune is here.

00:06:28.834 --> 00:06:30.300
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:30.300 --> 00:06:34.534
And we got great music from
Wizkid featuring Tems!

00:06:34.534 --> 00:06:36.534
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:38.868 --> 00:06:41.834
It was an exciting day
for me today.

00:06:41.834 --> 00:06:45.100
-So, what happened?
-Well, my song is out.

00:06:45.100 --> 00:06:47.868
I have a single out called
"It was a Masked Christmas."

00:06:47.868 --> 00:06:50.467
It's me --
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:50.467 --> 00:06:53.601
It's me and Ariana Grande and
Megan Thee Stallion.

00:06:53.601 --> 00:06:55.200
It's available on
any streaming service,

00:06:55.200 --> 00:06:56.501
anything you're listening to.

00:06:56.501 --> 00:06:59.534
But, so, I was doing
some press this morning,

00:06:59.534 --> 00:07:01.434
talking, which is rare,
'cause --

00:07:01.434 --> 00:07:03.734
Talking about my song,
which is fun.

00:07:03.734 --> 00:07:07.567
And I went to do "Elvis Duran
and the Morning," Z100.

00:07:07.567 --> 00:07:09.234
I love those guys,
the whole morning show.

00:07:09.234 --> 00:07:12.667
And I hadn't seen him
in person in over a year.

00:07:12.667 --> 00:07:14.634
You know, Zoom, maybe.

00:07:14.634 --> 00:07:15.968
It was great to see him.

00:07:15.968 --> 00:07:18.367
I was talking to him,
and they played the song.

00:07:18.367 --> 00:07:21.033
And I was like --
You know, I go,

00:07:21.033 --> 00:07:24.901
"It means so much to me
to hear my song on the radio,

00:07:24.901 --> 00:07:27.734
because I was a giant fan of
radio growing up."

00:07:27.734 --> 00:07:30.434
My dad -- My mom and dad
were so into radio.

00:07:30.434 --> 00:07:31.701
They just played it every day.

00:07:31.701 --> 00:07:34.100
My dad had me and my sister
climb into the attic

00:07:34.100 --> 00:07:36.767
to put wire
so that we can get reception.

00:07:36.767 --> 00:07:39.234
Totally safe.
-Yeah.

00:07:39.234 --> 00:07:42.901
-We get WCBS
and listen to "Cousin Brucie,"

00:07:42.901 --> 00:07:44.734
you know, in Saugerties,
New York, where we lived.

00:07:44.734 --> 00:07:48.434
You know, Norm N. Nite,
"Nite Train Show" or something.

00:07:48.434 --> 00:07:51.801
And I listened to -- Growing up,
K104 was my station,

00:07:51.801 --> 00:07:54.100
and Skywalker
does a good job there.

00:07:54.100 --> 00:07:55.334
But, anyways,
I'm talking to him about that

00:07:55.334 --> 00:07:57.033
and how much it means to me,
you know,

00:07:57.033 --> 00:08:00.167
to have my song
play on the radio.

00:08:00.167 --> 00:08:01.434
And he goes, "Alright, well,

00:08:01.434 --> 00:08:03.601
I know you're going back
to the office."

00:08:03.601 --> 00:08:05.534
'Cause, you know, We're down --
He's in New York.

00:08:05.534 --> 00:08:06.901
I go, "Yeah."

00:08:06.901 --> 00:08:09.400
He goes, "I'll give you a minute
to get out of the building

00:08:09.400 --> 00:08:10.634
and then tune into Z100

00:08:10.634 --> 00:08:13.234
so you can hear your song
on the radio."

00:08:13.234 --> 00:08:15.801
I just -- That was a cool move.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:08:15.801 --> 00:08:17.667
So, "Elvis Duran
and the Morning Show,"

00:08:17.667 --> 00:08:18.767
that was a class act.

00:08:18.767 --> 00:08:20.434
I appreciate that.
Thank you very much.

00:08:20.434 --> 00:08:23.667
Thank you iHeartRadio, too.
I appreciate it. That's awesome.

00:08:23.667 --> 00:08:25.133
"Masked Christmas," yeah.

00:08:25.133 --> 00:08:28.400
That was -- Oh.

00:08:28.400 --> 00:08:30.434
Oh, Tig Notaro. Tig, hey!

00:08:30.434 --> 00:08:32.801
[ Cheers and applause ]
♪♪

00:08:36.567 --> 00:08:40.067
Can I help you? Oh, my goodness.
-Oh, that's okay.

00:08:40.067 --> 00:08:42.767
I was just headed off
to the airport.

00:08:42.767 --> 00:08:45.300
Do you mind if I sit down?
-No, please. No, absolutely.

00:08:45.300 --> 00:08:48.567
Yeah. Tig Notaro, everybody.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:08:48.567 --> 00:08:49.968
You're off to the airport?
-Yeah.

00:08:49.968 --> 00:08:51.868
-You were just here
last night on our show.

00:08:51.868 --> 00:08:54.300
-Yeah. And It's also America's
Sweetheart Tig Notaro."

00:08:54.300 --> 00:08:56.534
-That's right.
I forgot to mention that.

00:08:58.033 --> 00:08:59.334
I forgot --
America's sweetheart.

00:08:59.334 --> 00:09:00.934
-Yeah, that's right.
-What's up, buddy?

00:09:00.934 --> 00:09:02.067
How can I help you?

00:09:02.067 --> 00:09:06.167
-Well, last night,
when I did your show,

00:09:06.167 --> 00:09:11.100
I had shown a picture of an
actress -- or just a celebrity.

00:09:11.100 --> 00:09:13.133
I didn't know who it was sitting
next to me on a flight.

00:09:13.133 --> 00:09:15.868
-That's correct.
-Do you have the picture still?

00:09:15.868 --> 00:09:17.868
-I do, from last night.
-Yeah.

00:09:17.868 --> 00:09:19.934
It's right there.

00:09:19.934 --> 00:09:21.534
-This is the photo, yeah.
-Yeah.

00:09:21.534 --> 00:09:23.267
-We were trying to guess
who the celebrity was.

00:09:23.267 --> 00:09:25.200
-We didn't know who it was.
-No, people were coming up

00:09:25.200 --> 00:09:27.300
to her the whole flight
and saying, "I love your work."

00:09:27.300 --> 00:09:29.267
-Yeah, they were like,
"Oh, even with a mask,

00:09:29.267 --> 00:09:31.167
I know who --"
Do you mind if I take this off?

00:09:31.167 --> 00:09:33.234
-No, it looks comfortable,
by the way.

00:09:33.234 --> 00:09:34.534
-Do you want to wear it?

00:09:34.534 --> 00:09:35.601
-No.
-Okay.

00:09:35.601 --> 00:09:37.334
[ Laughter ]

00:09:37.334 --> 00:09:40.434
But --
I'll be asleep soon.

00:09:40.434 --> 00:09:43.167
But they were like,
"Yeah, even with the mask,

00:09:43.167 --> 00:09:45.934
I know who you are
and the hair."

00:09:45.934 --> 00:09:47.300
-Yeah.
-And just the whole flight,

00:09:47.300 --> 00:09:49.167
I was like,
"Who the hell is this person?"

00:09:49.167 --> 00:09:52.200
-Yeah.
-And then you posted it online.

00:09:52.200 --> 00:09:53.467
-Yeah.
-Well, I guess you also

00:09:53.467 --> 00:09:56.100
aired your show.
Yeah.

00:09:56.100 --> 00:09:58.367
-Millions of people
watch our show, as well.

00:09:58.367 --> 00:10:00.801
-However you get
your "Tonight Show."

00:10:00.801 --> 00:10:02.968
-Yeah.
-This was online,

00:10:02.968 --> 00:10:05.434
and the Internet did its work.

00:10:05.434 --> 00:10:06.734
-Yeah, and they figured it out.

00:10:06.734 --> 00:10:12.968
-Figured out who it is.
And it is Rebecca Wisocky.

00:10:12.968 --> 00:10:15.000
-Rebecca Wisocky.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:10:15.000 --> 00:10:16.601
-Yeah.

00:10:16.601 --> 00:10:19.367
-She is on the show...
-Yeah. I -- Yeah.

00:10:19.367 --> 00:10:22.067
-She's on the show "Ghosts,"
on CBS.

00:10:22.067 --> 00:10:24.934
-Yeah, that's why I came by.
I came by --

00:10:24.934 --> 00:10:27.400
I came by --
Well, I came by on my way

00:10:27.400 --> 00:10:29.567
to the airport
to let you know that

00:10:29.567 --> 00:10:31.901
and to let everyone know

00:10:31.901 --> 00:10:35.267
that she's on "Ghosts,"
on CBS, at 9:00 p.m.

00:10:35.267 --> 00:10:38.033
[ Laughter, cheers, applause ]

00:10:38.033 --> 00:10:39.534
-Oh, good. I'm glad.
-On Thursday.

00:10:39.534 --> 00:10:41.133
-Thursday nights.
-Yeah, Thursday nights.

00:10:41.133 --> 00:10:42.534
-Tune in to CBS on Thursday.
Thanks, Tig.

00:10:42.534 --> 00:10:43.868
-Yeah.
-I appreciate this.

00:10:43.868 --> 00:10:46.033
-But I have to go.
-Have a safe --

00:10:46.033 --> 00:10:47.934
Have a safe flight.

00:10:47.934 --> 00:10:49.200
Tig Notaro, everybody.

00:10:49.200 --> 00:10:51.167
Thank you for coming by
and clearing that up.

00:10:51.167 --> 00:10:52.634
[ Cheers and applause ]
